{"chapter": "sets", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "000W", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\alpha$", "MATH_0002": "$\\text{Cov}(\\mathcal{C})_\\alpha$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-reflection-principle}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{remark-how-to-use-reflection}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-better}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dfee37ce4b9f55efb6d7a7722f698ebcc0b5da0c0f6befc6a4b5d62501905d62", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b09be2fda780128d9e998ad0d7cad9f918fe51ecf7e50aa8b39d1bc15ff0f062", "source_text": "It is likely the case that, for some limit ordinal <MATH_0001>,\nthe set of coverings <MATH_0002> satisfies\nthe conditions of the lemma. This is after all what an application\nof the reflection principle would appear to give (modulo caveats as\ndescribed at the end of Section <REF_0001>\nand in Remark <REF_0002>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:479f1bc7dffb7ac51f72ea458de5a8a49347f90290520114a6968758a624e872", "unit_id": "tag:000Y:statement"}
